{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_11-29-07-hashicorp_raft-real-run/agent-source && grep -n \\\"LeadershipTransferToServer\\\" -A 25 api.go | head -45; echo \\\"=== transfer handling ===\\\"; sed -n '740,790p' raft.go\"","aggregated_output":"1269:// LeadershipTransferToServer does the same as LeadershipTransfer but takes a\n1270-// server in the arguments in case a leadership should be transitioned to a\n1271-// specific server in the cluster.  Note that raft protocol version 3 is not\n1272-// sufficient to use LeadershipTransfer. A recent version of that library has\n1273-// to be used that includes this feature. Using transfer leadership is safe\n1274-// however in a cluster where not every node has the latest version. If a\n1275-// follower cannot be promoted, it will fail gracefully.\n1276:func (r *Raft) LeadershipTransferToServer(id ServerID, address ServerAddress) Future {\n1277-\tif r.protocolVersion < 3 {\n1278-\t\treturn errorFuture{ErrUnsupportedProtocol}\n1279-\t}\n1280-\n1281-\treturn r.initiateLeadershipTransfer(&id, &address)\n1282-}\n=== transfer handling ===\n\t\t\t\tcase err := <-doneCh:\n\t\t\t\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\t\t\t\tr.logger.Debug(err.Error())\n\t\t\t\t\t\tfuture.respond(err)\n\t\t\t\t\t} else {\n\t\t\t\t\t\t// Wait for up to ElectionTimeout before flagging the\n\t\t\t\t\t\t// leadership transfer as done and unblocking applies in\n\t\t\t\t\t\t// the leaderLoop.\n\t\t\t\t\t\tselect {\n\t\t\t\t\t\tcase <-time.After(r.config().ElectionTimeout):\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\terr := fmt.Errorf(\"leadership transfer timeout\")\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tr.logger.Debug(err.Error())\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tfuture.respond(err)\n\t\t\t\t\t\tcase <-leftLeaderLoop:\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tr.logger.Debug(\"lost leadership during transfer (expected)\")\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tfuture.respond(nil)\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t}()\n\n\t\t\t// leaderState.replState is accessed here before\n\t\t\t// starting leadership transfer asynchronously because\n\t\t\t// leaderState is only supposed to be accessed in the\n\t\t\t// leaderloop.\n\t\t\tid := future.ID\n\t\t\taddress := future.Address\n\t\t\tif id == nil {\n\t\t\t\ts := r.pickServer()\n\t\t\t\tif s != nil {\n\t\t\t\t\tid = &s.ID\n\t\t\t\t\taddress = &s.Address\n\t\t\t\t} else {\n\t\t\t\t\tdoneCh <- fmt.Errorf(\"cannot find peer\")\n\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tstate, ok := r.leaderState.replState[*id]\n\t\t\tif !ok {\n\t\t\t\tdoneCh <- fmt.Errorf(\"cannot find replication state for %v\", id)\n\t\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tr.setLeadershipTransferInProgress(true)\n\t\t\tgo r.leadershipTransfer(*id, *address, state, stopCh, doneCh)\n\n\t\tcase <-r.leaderState.commitCh:\n\t\t\tr.mainThreadSaturation.working()\n\t\t\t// Process the newly committed entries\n\t\t\toldCommitIndex := r.getCommitIndex()\n\t\t\tcommitIndex := r.leaderState.commitment.getCommitIndex()\n\t\t\tr.setCommitIndex(commitIndex)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
